{%- comment -%}
  sect-head — the eyebrow / heading / intro block that opens a section.

  Nine of the guide-library sections carry the same four settings —
  `show_head`, `eyebrow`, `heading`, `intro` — and rendered the same three
  elements from nine copies of the markup. One copy, here.

  Parameters:
    show     — the section's `show_head`. Anything falsy renders nothing.
    eyebrow  — small uppercase line above the heading
    heading  — the heading text. Rendered h2, flanked and centred by default
    intro    — a paragraph under the heading
    align    — 'center' (default) or 'left'
    flank    — false to drop the hairlines either side of the heading
    level    — 'h2' (default) or 'h3', for a section nested inside another

  Renders NOTHING when every text field is empty, so a section with no header
  set does not leave an empty flex box and a 48px margin behind.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign is_on = true
  if show == false
    assign is_on = false
  endif
  if eyebrow == blank and heading == blank and intro == blank
    assign is_on = false
  endif
  assign al = align | default: 'center'
  assign tag = level | default: 'h2'
-%}
{%- if is_on -%}
  <div class="sect-head{% if al == 'left' %} sect-head--left{% endif %}">
    {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if heading != blank -%}
      {%- if tag == 'h3' -%}
        <h3 class="{% if flank != false and al == 'center' %}heading-flank{% endif %}">{{ heading }}</h3>
      {%- else -%}
        <h2 class="{% if flank != false and al == 'center' %}heading-flank{% endif %}">{{ heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if intro != blank -%}
      <p class="lead">{{ intro }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
